    chore: make coverage floors reviewable make variables (BT-85)
    
    cover-check took --min-total=80 --min-package=60 as literal flags, so the only
    way to prove the gate is load-bearing was to edit the Makefile. The floors are
    now COVER_MIN_TOTAL / COVER_MIN_PACKAGE make variables (defaults unchanged),
    committed to internal/covercheck floors as the single place they live.
    
    Verified at this tree:
    - make cover-check -> total 83.1%, lowest package internal/describe 66.5%, PASS (14 packages), rc=0
    - make cover-check COVER_MIN_PACKAGE=95 -> rc non-zero, names 13 packages below floor
    - go build/vet/test -count=1 ./... rc=0; fmt-check, version-check v0.2.0, spec-check, vuln-check rc=0
    
